    "## TF-IDF Baseline with Cosine Similarity\n",
    "\n",
    "This baseline uses **Term Frequency–Inverse Document Frequency (TF-IDF)** to represent the textual content of the questions and answer options as numerical vectors. The TF-IDF vectorizer is trained on the combined text from the prompt and all five answer options to build a vocabulary of important terms.\n",
    "\n",
    "For each question, the prompt and each answer option are transformed into TF-IDF vectors. **Cosine similarity** is then computed between the prompt vector and each option vector, measuring their semantic similarity based on shared terms. The answer choices are ranked by similarity, and the **top three options** are selected as predictions.\n",
    "\n",
    "The model is evaluated on the training set using the **MAP@3** metric. Finally, predictions are generated for the test set and saved in the required submission format."
   ]
