    "### Error Analysis Insights\n",
    "\n",
    "The common leakage-free validation set contained 361 MCQs. BiLSTM produced the\n",
    "lowest number of Top-1 errors, with only 4 incorrect predictions (1.11% error\n",
    "rate). DistilBERT produced 41 errors (11.36%), while the RAG approach produced\n",
    "62 errors (17.17%).\n",
    "\n",
    "The three models disagreed on 94 validation questions, showing that the models\n",
    "learn different decision patterns. In several disagreement cases, BiLSTM\n",
    "predicted the correct option while either DistilBERT or RAG selected a different\n",
    "answer. RAG showed the highest error rate, indicating that retrieval and\n",
    "reranking do not always provide sufficiently relevant context for the final\n",
    "answer selection.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, BiLSTM was the strongest individual model on this validation split,\n",
    "while the differences in model predictions provide motivation for evaluating\n",
    "ensemble methods that combine complementary model outputs."
   ]
